doctype html
html(lang="en")
  head
    meta(charset="UTF-8")
    meta(name="viewport", content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0")
    title Sample Resume
    style.
      body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.6;
        margin: 20px;
      }
      .page {
        page-break-after: always;
      }
      h1, h2, h3, h4 {
        margin: 0;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: 16pt;
      }
      .contact-info p {
        margin: 0;
      }
      .section {
        margin-top: 15px;
      }
      .section h3 {
        border-bottom: 1px solid #000;
        padding-bottom: 2px;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }
      ul {
        list-style-type: disc;
        margin-left: 20px;
        padding-left: 0;
      }
      .job, .education-item, .leadership-item, .volunteer-item {
        margin-bottom: 15px;
      }
      .tips {
        background-color: #f0f0f0;
        border: 1px solid #ccc;
        padding: 10px;
        margin-top: 15px;
      }
      .tips h4 {
        margin-top: 0;
      }
  body
    //- Page 1
    .page
      header
        h1 FIRSTNAME LASTNAME
        .contact-info
          p 1457 Main St., Anytown, ON N7V 2Y1, 519 542 5551, c0555555@mylambton.ca
          p LinkedIn.com/in/FirstnameLastname

      section.section.objective
        h3 Objective
        p Seeking a position as Customer Service Representative at XYZCompany where I can contribute my proven proficiency in Microsoft Office along with skills in building strong customer relationships and handling multiple tasks efficiently.
        .tips
          h4 Tips:
          ul
            li Optional. One or two sentences. Specific to what you are applying to.
            li Focus on what you can do for the organization rather than what you are hoping they will do for you.
            li Consider job target & environment applying for, your key assets, and benefits to employer.
            li If you don't know what position you are applying for, consider using a Summary of Qualifications or About Me section highlighting your years of experience in the profession or industry, identifying your areas of expertise and personal attributes.

      section.section.education
        h3 Education
        .education-item
          p #[strong BUSINESS - ACCOUNTING]
          p Lambton College, Sarnia ON
          p #[em Dean's Honour List, GPA 3.9/4.0]
          p 2015
        .education-item
          p #[strong OFFICE ADMINISTRATION - GENERAL]
          p Lambton College, Sarnia ON
          p Sept. 2016 April 2018
        .tips
          h4 Tips:
          ul
            li List Lambton College your current school first, followed by previous schools, degrees, diplomas.
            li Add location of each school city and province. If you have an outstanding GPA you can include it, 3.5/4.0 or over or Dean's Honor List.
            li You can list your anticipated grad date as the end date.
            li If you are in your first year of your first post-secondary education, or want to include awards/recognition/scholarships you can list high school.
            li You can list relevant courses that are in line with the position you are applying to.

      section.section.skills
        h3 Skills and Qualifications
        ul
          li Effective computer skills - Microsoft Word, Excel, Power Point, Internet Research
          li Five years customer service experience
          li Fluent in verbal and written English, French and Spanish
          li Two years' experience organizing and implementing events
          li Valid CPR and First Aid Certificate
          li Smart Serve Certified
        .tips
          h4 Tips:
          ul
            li Optional. Can also be called Highlights of Qualifications. Strengths related to the position you are applying for.
            li 5-7 reasons you would be great for the position. List languages you know and level of proficiency i.e. basic, intermediate, advanced, fluent.

    //- Page 2
    .page
      header
        h2 FIRSTNAME LASTNAME

      section.section.related-experience
        h3 Related Experience
        .job
          h4 Clerk, ANY BUSINESS, Sarnia ON
          p 519 542 5551
          p #[em Sept. 2015 - Present]
          ul
            li Provide friendly and efficient customer service; professionally handle customer questions and concerns in a small family operated business
            li Demonstrate ability to build successful relationships with customers by listening carefully to needs and recommend the appropriate products
            li Display initiative to develop a computerized database which saved four hours per week from previous method and increased office efficiency
            li Operate cash register, handle and balance all debit, credit and cash transactions
            li Work efficiently under pressure with little or no supervision on night shifts
        .job
          h4 Office Assistant, ANY COMPANY, Anytown ON
          p #[em Summer 2015]
          ul
            li Reorganized the filing system for over 10,000 tax documents using a simplified colour coding system and saved time for administrative staff at the end of each month
            li Facilitated a presentation on how to use new systems and was commended by supervisor for public speaking and communication skills
            li Maintained positive client relations and dealt with conflict in a highly professional manner when contacting companies regarding overdue accounts and recovering outstanding debts
            li Pitched and cultivated a relationship with CompanyABC securing $10,000 partnership
            li Schedule weekly team meetings and communicated results to clients
        .tips
          h4 Tips:
          ul
            li Optional. Use accomplishment statements, not duties, proving that you can bring value to the organization by providing examples.
            li Begin statements with a skill action verb (i.e. advised, evaluated, collaborated.) Think about the action you took and the result that came from it, a time you made a difference, i.e. increased event participation, saved time or money, received recognition or an award, or organized an event with a successful outcome.
            li What was the challenge/issue/problem you faced?
            li What was the action you took/how did you respond/what skill you used?
            li What was the result/the benefit of your action? Quantify results when possible, $, #, %.
            li List your most recent experience first. If your most recent is your most relevant just use "work experience" section.
            li If your most recent is not your most relevant, you may want to consider creating a "Related Experience" section and putting your other experiences in "Work Experience" section.

      section.section.work-experience
        h3 Work Experience
        .job
          h4 Server, ANY RESTAURANT, Anycity ON
          p #[em 2014-2015]
          ul
            li Served food and beverage in the fine dining restaurant, maintaining a professional and friendly manner
            li Familiar with all menu items and offered recommendations for special diets and suggested additional items to increase restaurant sales
            li Effectively communicated with kitchen staff regarding customer allergies, dietary needs and other special requests

    //- Page 3
    .page
      header
        h2 FIRSTNAME LASTNAME
        p 519 542 5551
      
      .tips
        h4 Tips:
        p This experience may not be related directly to position you are applying for. Focus on transferable skills ie. Teamwork, customer service, initiative, working under pressure.

      section.section.leadership-experience
        h3 Leadership Experience
        .leadership-item
          h4 Student Council President, Lambton College, Sarnia ON
          p #[em Sept 2016 April 2017]
          ul
            li Led a team of four executive members, facilitated monthly meetings and planned weekly activities for over 20 members
            li Collaborated with five student groups to organize campus events which raised $2,000 for local charity
        .tips
          h4 Tips:
          ul
            li Optional. Include involvement showing leadership. Are you captain of a sports team? Leader of a club or project?
            li View ways to get involved via Co-Curricular opportunities https://mycareer.lambtoncollege.ca. CCR participation could also go under "Experience or "Volunteer Experience".

      section.section.volunteer-experience
        h3 Volunteer Experience
        .volunteer-item
          h4 Fundraising Assistant, United Way, Sarnia ON
          p #[em Summer 2016]
          ul
            li Recruited, coordinated and trained 14 volunteer fundraisers
            li Planned and promoted three successful fundraising events which generated over $20,000 in pledges
            li Developed and maintained twitter social media page
        .tips
          h4 Tips:
          ul
            li Optional. Many employers value volunteer experience. Showcase key skills. Related volunteer experience could be included under "Related Experience" section.
            li If including your volunteer in an "experience" section be sure to state volunteer.

      section.section.activities-interest
        h3 Activities/Interest
        ul
          li Solving complex coding issues, blogging on web development, and playing chess.
          
      section.section.additional-tips
        h3 Additional Tips:
        ul
          li You don't want your resume to be boring and look like everyone else's!
          li For formatting samples and ideas, check out https://lambton.optimalresume.com/, download to word for final edits and save.
          li Resume should be visually appealing and easy to follow. Keep formatting consistent throughout resume 1-2 pages. Print single sided.
          li Name at top should be approx. 16 pt. font. 11 pt. font is optimal size for body of resume.
          li Use easy to read font such as Arial. Use left justification. Margins should be even on both sides.
          li Use consistent format on other documents (cover letter, references).
          li Think about order or importance to the position you are applying for when listing headings/qualifications/accomplishments.
          li Within each section, list chronologically (most recent first).
          li Avoid abbreviations. If you abbreviate province or months do so throughout your resume.
          li Use appropriate verb tense i.e. presently doing this (research), completed task in the past (researched).
          li Update regularly.
          li Check all spelling and grammar, and have someone double check
          li Resume review appointments can be made via https://mycareer.lambtoncollege.ca
          li This is a sample and not to be copied